7592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1074 "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{9{\\pi }^{2}}=3\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=3$, we have ${\\omega }_{3}=3\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{3}=\\omega ,$ the $n=3$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=3$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x)=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{3}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x))+x(-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″} & =-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)-9{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+9{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)-9{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+9{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-6\\pi A=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ 6\\pi B=0\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}A=-\\frac{1}{27\\pi } \\\\ B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=-\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x).\n$$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397014 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397015 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397016 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397017 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1077 "field-1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397017 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1080 #uuid "6c917125-cff6-58cf-bd8e-53fff9587ed6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1081 "n=4" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1084 #uuid "718e9566-c7c9-5a9a-b62c-206f45871768" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1081 "n=1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1084 #uuid "4123d653-3eb6-56f8-9a54-2ef04840a633" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397016 1081 "n=2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397016 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397016 1084 #uuid "5c2e6e0a-4098-5507-86d3-f9eae8b3dec8" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397017 1081 "n=3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397017 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397017 1084 #uuid "d77b424d-712f-5538-af48-9fa7a0208031" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397018 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397019 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397018 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397020 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397018 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397021 1319413953